# Tools that build the Windows .exe (CI's exe job). Edit this file, then regenerate
# requirements-build.txt on Windows, where the .exe is built: some of PyInstaller's
# dependencies (pefile, pywin32-ctypes) are only resolved there.
#   python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --strip-extras --no-emit-index-url requirements-build.in
# Both files are installed together, so every package they share must have the
# same pin: the constraint below makes this file reuse the pins of requirements.txt.

-c requirements.txt

pyinstaller
